A good pit latrine:

1. is built **far from water sources** (wells, streams) and away from the kitchen, to avoid contamination of water and food;
2. has a **deep pit** with strong, lined walls, to avoid collapse and to take a long time to fill;
3. has a **tight-fitting cover or lid** over the hole and a **slab** with a smooth, washable floor;
4. has a **ventilation pipe** covered with a fly screen, to remove smell and prevent flies and mosquitoes from breeding;
5. has a **roof and walls** (door) giving privacy and protection from rain;
6. is **kept clean**, with a place for washing hands after use;
7. is built on **high ground**, not in flood-prone areas, and is easily accessible.

(Any six.)
